- All stock checks happen before any debit: unknown SKUs or insufficient total stock raise ValueError and change neither stocks nor requests. Rejected requests may later succeed with valid items.
- A receipt has items (the normalized dict) and status ('reserved' or 'released'). Returned receipts must not expose mutable internal state.
- release restores stock once; repeated release returns the released receipt without restoring again. An unknown tenant/request key raises KeyError. Replaying a released reservation returns the released receipt and does not reacquire stock.
- Tenant stocks and request IDs are isolated. The constructor must not mutate the supplied stock mapping.

